    "title": "Special Weather Statement by NWS - NewsBreak",
    "text": "Check NWS updates here At 1006 PM CDT, Doppler radar was tracking strong thunderstorms along a line extending from 8 miles north of Arnold to near Stapleton. Movement was southeast at 35 mph. HAZARD...Wind gusts up to 50 mph and half inch hail. SOURCE...Radar indicated. IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around unsecured objects. Minor hail damage to vegetation is possible. Strong thunderstorms will be near... Gandy around 1010 PM CDT. Arnold around 1015 PM CDT. Other locations impacted by these storms include Tarboz Lake, Shanklin Bluff, Pleasant Hill, Etna, Logan, Hoagland, Milldale, Finchville, and Lodi. This includes the following highways... Highway 92 between mile markers 219 and 263. Highway 83 between mile markers 96 and 122.",
